{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgucKwLssGRE9fVv8Zz66","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`, and it's the only file I created. I haven't run it or checked it against a Camel 4.22 runtime. The option names below come from the Camel Kafka component as I know it.\n\n**Record key:** a `setHeader` step copies `${header.orderId}` into the `kafka.KEY` header, and the Kafka producer uses that header as the record key. I did it this way because the endpoint's own `key` option takes a fixed value. It can't read a header from each message.\n\n**Kafka endpoint** (`kafka:orders.accepted`):\n- `brokers: \"{{kafka.brokers}}\"` takes the broker list from the `kafka.brokers` property.\n- `enableIdempotence: true` makes the producer idempotent.\n- `requestRequiredAcks: all` waits for all in-sync replicas to acknowledge. This is already the default in Camel 4, but I set it explicitly because idempotence depends on it.\n- `compressionCodec: lz4` turns on lz4 compression."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":720,"cache_read_input_tokens":4560,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":720},"output_tokens":339,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d20102b-b378-43ab-ae90-c16b6af875d8","uuid":"33525c3b-5953-4a3e-9816-171ac584f669","timestamp":"2026-11-10T17:04:08.386Z","request_id":"req_011CgucKw8jTC26ZyhTjcZqw"}
